{"metadata":{"description":"MCP bridge that lets ChatGPT web create, view, continue, and control DeepSeek Harness (DSH) agent sessions.","id":"gh:1334114196","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-chatgpt-bridge","slug":"jiezeng2004-design/dsh-chatgpt-bridge","topics":["chatgpt","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","mcp","model-context-protocol"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"MCP bridge that lets ChatGPT web create, view, continue, and control DeepSeek Harness (DSH) agent se"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"dge that lets ChatGPT web create, view, continue, and control DeepSeek Harness (DSH) agent sessions."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-chatgpt-bridge"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> **Let ChatGPT drive your local DSH agents.**
>
> 在 ChatGPT 里创建任务、继续会话、监督 Goal、处理审批并检查结果，不用在 ChatGP"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"T 和 DSH 之间反复复制 Prompt。"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"`dsh-chatgpt-bridge` connects **ChatGPT Web → secure MCP tunnel → DeepSeek Harness (DSH)**. ChatGPT "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"becomes the control surface; DSH keeps the agent loop, tools, skills, subagents, workflows, sandbox,"},{"id":"p4s3","text":" approvals and workspace security model."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**The bridge connects the two sides. It does not replace DSH, modify DSH core, or route DSH model tr"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"affic through ChatGPT.**"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Published **0.6.0** targets DSH **0.1.7-rc.2** exactly. The unpublished working tree now targets **0"},{"id":"p6s2","text":".2.0-rc.2**, with local tests and packed official CLI/Web/MCP acceptance passing on 2026-10-08. The "},{"id":"p6s3","text":"package version has not been bumped or republished. See the current compatibility evidence and publi"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"shed-release evidence. After a successful connection, ChatGPT should see **tool count = 23**."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Why this exists"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"A normal ChatGPT + local-agent workflow has too much manual glue:"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"With the bridge:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"You stay in ChatGPT while DSH remains the execution engine."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## What you can do from ChatGPT"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- create and inspect native DSH sessions;
- send follow-up instructions without copying context betw"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"een apps;
- start, inspect, update and wait on Goals;
- approve DSH actions through the bridge when "},{"id":"p14s3","text":"your DSH policy requires it;
- list registered workspaces and inspect runtime health;
- keep using D"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"SH's own sandbox, approval and workspace boundaries;
- manage the supported tunnel runtime from the "},{"id":"p14s5","text":"DSH Web settings UI."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Real setup"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"The screenshot is from a real DSH Web installation with sensitive values masked."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### Requirements"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- Node.js 22+
- DeepSeek Harness `0.1.7-rc.2` (`dsh` on `PATH`)
- a DSH Web profile/runtime
- ChatGP"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"T access that can use the currently supported MCP/custom-app connection flow"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### 1. Install the plugin"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Install v0.6.0 into the matching DSH 0.1.7-rc.2 host:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"To install from a reviewed source checkout instead:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Source installation into a real profile was not part of release verification. Back up the profile be"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"fore upgrading DSH: DSH owns V3 session migration. `npm install dsh-chatgpt-bridge` alone is not eno"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"ugh: the plugin must be added to a DSH profile bundle. Published v0.5.1 remains tied to the older DS"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"st be added to a DSH profile bundle. Published v0.5.1 remains tied to the older DSH 0.1.1-rc.2 host."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"### 2. Start DSH Web"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Keep DSH Web and the bridge in the **same web profile/runtime** so ChatGPT-created sessions appear l"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"nd the bridge in the **same web profile/runtime** so ChatGPT-created sessions appear live in the UI."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Default local endpoints:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"| Service | Endpoint |"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"| DSH Web | `http://127.0.0.1:3080` |
| Bridge MCP | `http://127.0.0.1:3456/mcp` |"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"### 3. Read the bridge token"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"Windows PowerShell:"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"macOS / Linux:"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"Treat this token like a password. Do not commit it, post it, or paste it into public chats."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"Alternatively, set `DSH_CHATGPT_BRIDGE_TOKEN` yourself and the bridge uses it instead of generating "},{"id":"p38s2","text":"tively, set `DSH_CHATGPT_BRIDGE_TOKEN` yourself and the bridge uses it instead of generating a file."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"### 4. Connect ChatGPT"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"ChatGPT Web cannot reach a plain localhost MCP endpoint directly. Use the secure MCP/tunnel connecti"},{"id":"p40s2","text":"on mechanism currently supported by OpenAI and forward it to:"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"Use the bridge token as the MCP bearer credential where the connection flow requires it."},{"id":"p43s1","text":"The bridge keeps a localhost-first design: it binds `127.0.0.1`, never exposes a public interface, a"},{"id":"p43s2","text":"nd never self-hosts a tunnel."},{"id":"p44s1","text":"### 5. Refresh tools and verify"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"After connecting, refresh/rescan the MCP tools in ChatGPT and run a read-only check:"},{"id":"p46s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p47s1","text":"A healthy first check should look like:"},{"id":"p48s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p49s1","text":"If health is OK, the version matches, and your registered workspace appears, the control path is rea"},{"id":"p49s2","text":"health is OK, the version matches, and your registered workspace appears, the control path is ready."},{"id":"p50s1","text":"## First useful workflow"},{"id":"p51s1","text":"A practical pattern is:"},{"id":"p52s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p53s1","text":"For a safe first run, start with a read-only Goal:"},{"id":"p54s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p55s1","text":"## Security model"},{"id":"p56s1","text":"This is a **control bridge**, not a remote shell replacement."},{"id":"p57s1","text":"- The MCP server binds to loopback by default.
- It binds `127.0.0.1`, never exposes a public interf"},{"id":"p57s2","text":"ace, and never self-hosts a tunnel.
- DSH remains responsible for its own sandbox, approvals and wor"},{"id":"p57s3","text":"kspace rules.
- The bridge only works with workspaces already registered in DSH.
- Tokens and tunnel"},{"id":"p57s4","text":"/runtime secrets are stored outside the repository and should never be committed.
- Write/action too"},{"id":"p57s5","text":"ls are real actions. Keep approval policies appropriate for the workspace you expose.
- Tunnel/runti"},{"id":"p57s6","text":"me management is designed to fail closed around process ownership and lifecycle ambiguity."},{"id":"p58s1","text":"If you only need inspection, use read-only prompts and keep DSH constraints read-only."},{"id":"p59s1","text":"## What this project is not"},{"id":"p60s1","text":"- It is **not** a ChatGPT API proxy.
- It does **not** make DSH use your ChatGPT subscription as a m"},{"id":"p60s2","text":"odel provider.
- It does **not** upload an arbitrary workspace to ChatGPT.
- It does **not** bypass "},{"id":"p60s3","text":"DSH approvals or sandboxing.
- It does **not** modify DeepSeek Harness core."},{"id":"p61s1","text":"## Troubleshooting"},{"id":"p62s1","text":"### ChatGPT cannot connect"},{"id":"p63s1","text":"`127.0.0.1` only exists on your machine. Confirm that your supported secure tunnel/MCP connection fo"},{"id":"p63s2","text":"rwards to the bridge endpoint and that the bridge token matches the running DSH profile."},{"id":"p64s1","text":"### `401 Unauthorized`"},{"id":"p65s1","text":"Re-read the token from the active DSH home/profile and make sure the connector sends the matching be"},{"id":"p65s2","text":"n from the active DSH home/profile and make sure the connector sends the matching bearer credential."}],"truncated":true}
